# Signal Racer BTS

Stage 5 uses audio as a timing metaphor, but the implementation keeps the required action deterministic.

The calibration loop records continuous listening against `transmission_hum.mp3` and unlocks `5.counter_wave_calibrated` after a full clean loop. The UI exposes a compact simulation control so tests and keyboard users can drive the same canonical path without depending on real media playback timing.

The Jammer boss remains locked until that action exists. After calibration, the race resolves immediately as a vertical slice of the final design.
